cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Coherent Object (FTGB): a driven Beltrami-Hopf toroidal soliton, read as field and matter wave"
abstract: >
  A reproducible, honestly-tiered synthesis around one driven, force-free Beltrami-Hopf toroidal
  soliton, read at once as a plasma field and a Madelung matter wave. The verified core is a set of
  plasma / topological-fluid results (the Chandrasekhar-Kendall carrier spectrum; the R2 near-Beltrami
  enstrophy / BKM conditional-regularity theorem; the R3 Hall-MHD Pm-not-equal-1 coupled-Lyapunov lift;
  exact-state global regularity, where the object's nonlinearity is null at coherence; the topological
  invariants Q_H = 1 and Chern C = +/-2; the Beltrami = Reeb-field contact structure with Weinstein-Taubes
  closed-orbit existence; the chirality / charge-conjugation / Majorana cluster; the S^3 curl spectral
  zeta; the N-mode Woltjer linear-program theorem, by which a beat-carrying multi-mode structure is never
  a static minimum -- "heartbeat, not flywheel" is generic). The theory also runs as software: a full
  nonlinear pseudo-spectral Navier-Stokes simulation tracks the exact eternal Beltrami solution to ~5e-16,
  plus the CK comb/beat, driven-resonance, and de Broglie matter-wave packet dynamics
  (engine/ftgb_resonator_sim.py). A tiered knowledge layer preserves the plasmoid / EVO / cold-fusion
  science history with its fences (HISTORY_PEOPLE_EVO_CMNS.md; vendored verified citation stores). Around
  the core sits a disciplined, tiered speculative frontier (the matter-wave particle reading, the alpha
  value as a settled-negative, LENR energetics, the lepton mass tower). Every load-bearing claim is
  reproduced by a script (verify_all.py, 91/91, CI-gated); no claim exceeds its tier; settled-negatives
  are kept as wins.
type: software
